{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-135993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${(1-\\frac{b}{3})}^{8}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037372/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7ed5460e635fa5a773edf06dc3b4336b32e29d59140e6a93421a054a80958e2"} {"question" "q-135993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-\\frac{b}{3}$ and $n=8$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-\\frac{b}{3})}^{8} & =1+8\\cdot (-\\frac{b}{3})+\\frac{8(8-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{b}{3})}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8b}{3}+\\frac{8\\cdot 7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{b}^{2}}{9}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8b}{3}+28\\cdot \\frac{{b}^{2}}{9}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8b}{3}+\\frac{28{b}^{2}}{9}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037372/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7ed5460e635fa5a773edf06dc3b4336b32e29d59140e6a93421a054a80958e2"} {"question" "q-135993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037372/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1efaf6c3080d3dc33f36950bb4b8b3ca678b008eb2878226c653253ed685871c"} {"question" "q-135993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037372/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7ed5460e635fa5a773edf06dc3b4336b32e29d59140e6a93421a054a80958e2"} {"question" "q-135993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\frac{8b}{3}+\\frac{29{b}^{2}}{9}+⋯"] ["math" "1+\\frac{8b}{3}+\\frac{32{b}^{2}}{9}+⋯"] [